<section class="leak-signs" aria-labelledby="leak-signs-title">
  <div class="signs-layout">
    <div class="signs-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Check your home</p>
      <h2 id="leak-signs-title">Signs You Have a Hidden Leak</h2>
      <p class="signs-intro">You usually don't see the water itself. You see the side effects. Any one of these is worth a phone call. Two or more usually means you have a hidden leak that needs attention before it gets expensive.</p>

      <ul class="signs-list">
        <li>A water bill jump you can't explain</li>
        <li>A damp or warm spot on the floor</li>
        <li>A musty smell that won't go away</li>
        <li>Mold or mildew where it shouldn't be</li>
        <li>Running water sounds with every fixture off</li>
        <li>Low pressure at one or two faucets</li>
        <li>A yard patch that stays green in a dry week</li>
        <li>New cracks in floors or the foundation</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <aside class="urgent-steps" aria-labelledby="urgent-title">
      <h3 id="urgent-title">What to Do Right Now</h3>
      <ol>
        <li><span class="step-number">1</span><p><strong>Shut off the main water valve.</strong> It's usually where the line enters the house, in a crawl space, garage, or basement, or at the meter box by the street.</p></li>
        <li><span class="step-number">2</span><p><strong>Turn off the water heater</strong> if the leak looks like hot water or is near the tank.</p></li>
        <li><span class="step-number">3</span><p><strong>Kill power to wet areas</strong> at the breaker if water is near outlets or appliances.</p></li>
        <li><span class="step-number">4</span><p><strong>Smell gas? Get out first,</strong> then call your gas utility from outside.</p></li>
        <li><span class="step-number">5</span><p><strong><a href="tel:+17706797705">Call (770) 679-7705.</a></strong> We answer 24/7 with no after-hours surcharge.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

